(several parts on one sheet)
(PureCutCNC reference program for the QtPlasmaC simulator check, issue #954.)
(Hand-written from the QtPlasmaC manual for LinuxCNC 2.9; each stanza names)
(the manual section it comes from. See ../README.md.)

(Manual: Preamble and Postamble Codes)
G21 G40 G49 G64 P0.1 G80 G90 G92.1 G94 G97
(Manual: Paused Motion)
M52 P1
(Manual: Automatic Material Handling - select, wait, then take the feed rate)
(from the material; the three codes must come in this order)
M190 P1
M66 P3 L3 Q1
F#<_hal[plasmac.cut-feed-rate]>

(Three parts nested on one sheet. Each part is finished - holes, then)
(outline - before the torch moves on to the next.)

(part A: 60 x 40 rectangle)
G0 X15 Y40
M3 $0 S1
G1 X20 Y40
G1 X20 Y60
G1 X80 Y60
G1 X80 Y20
G1 X20 Y20
G1 X20 Y40
M5 $0

(part B: 50 mm disc, centre X130 Y45, clockwise)
G0 X100 Y45
M3 $0 S1
G1 X105 Y45
G2 X105 Y45 I25 J0
M5 $0

(part C: 70 x 60 plate with a 36 mm hole, centre X55 Y110)
G0 X55 Y110
M3 $0 S1
G1 X73 Y110
G3 X73 Y110 I-18 J0
M5 $0
G0 X15 Y110
M3 $0 S1
G1 X20 Y110
G1 X20 Y140
G1 X90 Y140
G1 X90 Y80
G1 X20 Y80
G1 X20 Y110
M5 $0

(Manual: Preamble and Postamble Codes)
G0 X0 Y0
G21 G40 G49 G64 P0.1 G80 G90 G92.1 G94 G97
